window.docContents[65].resolve({"/Elementary-Functions/Chapter-contents/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Elementary-Functions--Chapter-contents--Trigonometric-functions":{"contents":"* 4.14 Definitions and Periodicity* 4.15 Graphics* 4.16 Elementary Properties* 4.17 Special Values and Limits* 4.18 Inequalities* 4.19 Maclaurin Series and Laurent Series* 4.20 Derivatives and Differential Equations* 4.21 Identities* 4.22 Infinite Products and Partial Fractions* 4.23 Inverse Trigonometric Functions* 4.24 Inverse Trigonometric Functions: Further Properties* 4.25 Continued Fractions* 4.26 Integrals* 4.27 Sums\n\n","context":"LMLF · DLMF with Lean\u0009Elementary Functions\u0009Chapter contents","header":"Trigonometric functions","id":"/Elementary-Functions/Chapter-contents/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Elementary-Functions--Chapter-contents--Trigonometric-functions"},"/Elementary-Functions/___4___37-Inverse-Hyperbolic-Functions/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Elementary-Functions--___4___37-Inverse-Hyperbolic-Functions--___4___37-Inverse-Hyperbolic-Functions--Logarithmic-forms":{"contents":"Source: DLMF §4.37(iv)\n\nE16–E25 state principal logarithmic expressions off their cuts and the\nupper/lower boundary values on the cuts. E16 allows the endpoints ±i; its\nexcluded intervals are open. E19 and E21 use ℂ \\ (-∞,1) for the formula,\nwhile the analytic cut is (-∞,1]. The branch-aware arccoshRadical is the\ntwo-square-root realization of E19's ± sign (and E21's equivalent formula).\nThe CutSide values make both signs in E17, E18, E22, E23, and E25 explicit;\nMathlib's totalized Complex.log is single-valued and cannot itself represent\nboth DLMF boundary limits. DLMF notes that the principal square root in E19 is\ndiscontinuous on the imaginary axis, so analytic continuation switches to the\nother branch; this explains the ± sign. The subsection also points to\nDempsey (2025) for more concrete principal-branch expressions.\n\n\n\n","context":"LMLF · DLMF with Lean\u0009Elementary Functions\u0009§4.37 Inverse Hyperbolic Functions\u0009§4.37 Inverse Hyperbolic Functions","header":"Logarithmic forms","id":"/Elementary-Functions/___4___37-Inverse-Hyperbolic-Functions/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Elementary-Functions--___4___37-Inverse-Hyperbolic-Functions--___4___37-Inverse-Hyperbolic-Functions--Logarithmic-forms"}});